          "term": "frac x-y",
          "heading": false
        }
      ],
      "extract": "In this section, we prove that the Möbius energy of a knot is bounded by the ropelength. Our goal is partly the theorem itself and partly the paradigm: any \"energy\" defined in terms of inverse-square distances should have an analogous bound, with the proof following this model. ::: thm If $K$ is a smooth knot in $\\Rset^3$ then $$E_{O4}(K) < 4.57\\, E_L(K)^{4/3}. \\label{powbound}$$ []{#main label=\"main\"} ::: ::: thm",
      "extractCut": true
    }
